{
  "query": "# TASK-204: RingBuffer Capacity Enforcement and Overflow Detection\n\n## Summary\nUnder high load, memory metrics indicated that `RingBuffer` exceeded its configured capacity threshold before raising a `BufferOverflowError`, causing memory bloat in storage buffering.\n\n## Current Observed Behavior\n`RingBuffer.push()` permits `capacity + 1` items to be appended before throwing an overflow error due to an off-by-one boundary comparison.\n\n## Expected Behavior\nWhen the buffer already contains `capacity` items, attempting to push an additional item must immediately raise `BufferOverflowError(\"Buffer capacity exceeded\")`.\n",
